@group
    @title=Documentation Project Files
    @brief=The section described the documentation project files
    @ingroup=index
    @key=projectFile

    There are two kind of the project files 
    you need to create in order to successfully 
    compile a documentation project:

    1) A msbuild project file that calls all required actions

    2) A docgen project file that sets the source of the documentation
    and defines the desired documentation output.
@end

@group
    @title=Documentation project
    @brief=The section describes XML file defining the documentation project
    @key=docProjectFile
    @ingroup=projectFile

    The documentation project file defines:

    * The common properties of the project
    * The location of the source files and compiler rules
    * The output templates to be used and their parameters

    Follow the project file scheme to define the project content.

    The root element of the project file is [clink=docProjectFile1.help-project]help-project[/clink].
@end

@class
    @name=project.xml file
    @brief=The section describes XML file defining the documentation project
    @key=docProjectFile1
    @ingroup=docProjectFile
    @type=tags
    @membersToContent=true

    The project file is an XML file that must
    use the namespace [c]http://www.gehtsoft.com/docgen/project[/c]
    The root tag of the project file must be [c]help-project[/c].

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=help-project
        @brief=The root element of the project document
        @custom=xml-tag
        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=
        @end

        Don't forget to add reference to the namespace
        [c]http://www.gehtsoft.com/docgen/project[/c]
        and, if a prefix is used, keep prefix use
        consitent trough the whole project file.

        @example
            @show=yes
            @title=Project file example
            @highlight=xml
            @tabs=yes
            @tab
                @title=Without namespace prefix
                ```
                <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
                 <help-project xmlns="http://www.gehtsoft.com/docgen/project">
                 [i]... project content ...[/i]
                </help-project>
                ```
                @end
            @tab
                @title=With namespace prefix
                ```
                <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
                 <dg:help-project xmlns:dg="http://www.gehtsoft.com/docgen/project">
                 [i]... project content ...[/i]
                </dg:help-project>
                ```
            @end
        @end

        The project may have three sections:

        * Optional common definitions section (see [clink=docProjectFile1.common]common[/clink])
        * One source section (see [clink=docProjectFile1.source]source[/clink])
        * One or more output template sections (see [clink=docProjectFile1.output]output[/clink])
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=common
        @brief=The tag consists of the definitions that are common for all templates and for the parser
        @custom=xml-tag
        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=
        @end

        The tag may be used once inside of
        [clink=docProjectFile1.help-project]help-project[/clink] tag.

        The tag may contain one or more
        [clink=docProjectFile1.define]define[/clink] tags.
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=source
        @brief=The tag consists of source files and folders
        @custom=xml-tag
        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=
        @end
        The tag should be used once inside of
        [clink=docProjectFile1.help-project]help-project[/clink] tag.

        The tag may contain one or more
        [clink=docProjectFile1.file]file[/clink] and/or
        [clink=docProjectFile1.folder]folder[/clink] tags.

        The files and folders will be processed in the order
        in which they are specified in the [c]source[/c]
        tag.
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=output
        @brief=The tags defines the output template to be used
        @custom=xml-tag
        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=template="[i]path[/i]" output="[i]file[/i]" encoding="[i]encoding[/i]"
        @end

        The tag should be used one or more time inside of
        [clink=docProjectFile1.help-project]help-project[/clink] tag.

        The section may contain one or more
        [clink=docProjectFile1.define]define[/clink] tags.
        for template-specific definitions.

        Refer the template documentation of the list
        of the templates available and for the
        parameters specific for the template.

        @param
            @name=template
            The name of the main file in the template.

            If you build your help file with a standard template
            and using nuget package (e.g. via MSBuild)
            you can refer to a standard templates using
            [c]%docgen%/template/[/c] as the base path.
        @end

        @param
            @name=output
            The name of the output file (for templates
            that creates only one file).

            For templates that creates multiple file use
            this parameter to specify the output folder.
            However, because the parameter requires a file,
            add [c]null-file[/c] as a file name. The file
            with such name will not be created, however, its
            location will be used as base path to create
            all other files by the template.
        @end

        @param
            @name=encoding
            The name of the encoding for output file(s) (e.g. 'ascii', 'utf-8', or 'windows-1252').
        @end
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=define
        @brief=The tag defines a constant.
        @custom=xml-tag
        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=name="[i]name[/i]" value="[i]value[/i]"
        @end


        The tag may be used inside
        [clink=docProjectFile1.common]common[/clink] or
        [clink=docProjectFile1.output]output[/clink] elements.

        @param
            @name=name
            The name of the constant.
        @end
        @param
            @name=value
            The constant value.
        @end
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=file
        @brief=The tag defines an input file
        @custom=xml-tag
        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=name="[i]relative path[/i]" encoding="[i]encoding name[/i]"
        @end

        The tag may be used inside
        [clink=docProjectFile1.source]source[/clink] tag.

        @param
            @name=name
            The relative path to the file from the folder that contains [c]project.xml[/c] file.
        @end
        @param
            @name=encoding
            The name of the file encoding (e.g. 'ascii', 'utf-8', or 'windows-1252').
        @end

    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=folder
        @brief=The tag defines a source folder.
        @custom=xml-tag

        All files with extension .ds in the folder specified will be included.
        There is no warranty about the particular order in which the
        files will be processed. If you need to handle your files
        in particular order - use [clink=docProjectFile1.file]file[/clink]
        tag to include each file individually.

        The tag may be used inside
        [clink=docProjectFile1.source]source[/clink] tag.

        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=name="[i]relative path[/i]" encoding="[i]encoding name[/i]"
        @end

        @param
            @name=name
            The relative path to the folder from the folder that contains [c]project.xml[/c] file.
        @end
        @param
            @name=encoding
            The name of the file encoding (e.g. 'ascii', 'utf-8', or 'windows-1252').
        @end
    @end
@end

@group
    @title=MSBuild Project File
    @brief=The section describes MSBuild file defining the project compilation routing
    @ingroup=projectFile
    @key=msbuildProjectFile

    The build file is a standard
    [eurl=https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/msbuild/msbuild]MSBuild[/eurl]
    project file. This file may be compiled using either [c]msbuild.exe[/c]
    or [c]dotnet build[/c] command.

    The docgen relies on two nuget packages available
    from Gehtsoft public nuget stream
    [eurl=https://www.myget.org/F/gehtsoft-public/api]https://www.myget.org/F/gehtsoft-public/api/v3/index.json[/eurl]:

    * Gehtsoft.Build.DocGen
    * Gehtsoft.Build.ContentDelivery

    You organizes the build process using
    custom tasks defined in these packages. Refer to
    project tags for details about the tasks.

    You can also expand an example of a project files below
    that uses all custom tasks:

    @example
        @title=Documentation Project File Example
        @show=no
        @tabs=yes
        @tab
            @title=project
            @highlight=xml
            ```
            <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
            <Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
             <PropertyGroup>
              <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
             </PropertyGroup>
             <!-- Get required packages -->
             <ItemGroup>
              <!-- If you update the package version here,
                   don't forget to update it as well below,
                   In ContentFromPackage task parameters -->
              <PackageReference Include="Gehtsoft.Build.DocGen" Version="0.1.12" IncludeAssets="build" />
              <PackageReference Include="Gehtsoft.Build.ContentDelivery" Version="0.1.10" IncludeAssets="build" />
             </ItemGroup>
             <!-- Define folder location -->
             <PropertyGroup>
              <DocTargetDir>$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/dst</DocTargetDir>
             </PropertyGroup>
             <!-- Define file groups and constants -->
             <ItemGroup>
              <!-- Images and raw HTML files to include into doc -->
              <CustomFile Include="$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/img/**/*.png;$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/html/**/*.*" />
              <!-- All files in target directory -->
              <CurrentDocTargetDir Include="$(DocTargetDir)" />
             </ItemGroup>
             <!-- Target that removes results of compilation -->
             <Target Name="CleanDoc">
              <RemoveDir Directories="@(CurrentDocTargetDir)" />
             </Target>
             <!-- Target that creates the project -->
             <Target Name="MakeDoc">
              <!-- Remove previous output -->
              <RemoveDir Directories="@(CurrentDocTargetDir)" />
              <MakeDir Directories="$(DocTargetDir)" />
              <!-- Compile documentation project -->
              <DocGen Project="project.xml" />
              <!-- Copy raw content to the output folder -->
              <Copy SourceFiles="@(CustomFile)" DestinationFolder="$(DocTargetDir)" />
              <!-- Copy content (e.g. web menu, icons, scripts) for HTML template output -->
              <ContentFromPackage Package="Gehtsoft.Build.DocGen" Source="Content/template/html/res" Version="0.1.12" Destination="$(DocTargetDir)/res" />
              <ContentFromPackage Package="Gehtsoft.Build.DocGen" Source="Content/template/html/highlighter" Version="0.1.12" Destination="$(DocTargetDir)/highlighter" />
              <ContentFromPackage Package="Gehtsoft.Build.DocGen" Source="Content/template/html/menu" Version="0.1.12" Destination="$(DocTargetDir)/menu" />
              <ContentFromPackage Package="Gehtsoft.Build.DocGen" Source="Content/template/html/pageImages" Version="0.1.12" Destination="$(DocTargetDir)/pageImages" />
             </Target>
            </Project>
            ```
        @end
        @tab
            @title=Command
            ![c]dotnet build project.proj /t:CleanDoc,MakeDoc[/c]
        @end
    @end
@end

@class
    @name=Tasks
    @brief=The section describes custom MSBuild tasks
    @key=msbuildTasks
    @ingroup=msbuildProjectFile
    @type=tags
    @membersToContent=true

    @member
        @type=property
        @custom=xml-tag
        @name=ContentFromPackage
        @brief=The custom task copies content from a package folder to the specified folder

        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=Package="" Version="" Source=""  Destination=""
        @end

        @param
            @name=Package
            The name of the package, e.g. [c]gehtsoft.build.docgen[/c]

            In order to make it operable in Linux make sure
            that you use all lowercase in the package name!
        @end
        @param
            @name=Version
            The version of the package, e.g. [c]0.1.12[/c]

            When you are copying from [c]gehtsoft.build.docgen[/c]
            don't forget update the version in this task every time
            when you update the version in project reference.
        @end
        @param
            @name=Source
            The folder inside the package to copy data from.

            In order to make operable in Linux, use [c]/[/c]
            as path separator.
        @end
        @param
            @name=Destination
            The folder to copy data to.

            In order to make operable in Linux, use [c]/[/c]
            as path separator.
        @end
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @custom=xml-tag
        @name=DocGen
        @brief=The custom task that performs docgen project compilation

        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=Project=""
        @end

        @param
            @name=Project
            The path to the project file to compile
        @end
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @custom=xml-tag
        @name=Asm2Xml
        @brief=The custom task that scans .NET assemblies and creates an XML file with description of all types

        @declaration
            @language=xml
            @params=Assemblies="" OutputXml="" Mode="net5.0"
        @end

        @param
            @name=Assemblies
            The list of the assemblies to compile.

            Use MSBuild item list as the value of this parameter.
        @end

        @param
            @name=OutputXml
            The path to the output XML file with
            assemblies content.

            You can use [clink=cs2dsTemplate]cs2ds[/clink] template
            to create the documentation from this file. 
        @end
    @end
@end